{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation","imports":["lean:module:Init"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.symmetrizedSeifertDet_eq_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.symmetrizedSeifertDet_eq_three","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L112-L113","doc":"**`det(V + Vᵀ) = 3 = trefoil determinant`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.symmetrizedSeifertDet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.symmetrizedSeifertDet","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L109-L110","doc":"`det(V + Vᵀ)` for `V + Vᵀ = [[-2,1],[1,-2]]`: `(-2)(-2) − (1)(1) = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.relator_abelianises_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.relator_abelianises_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L95-L100","doc":"**The genus-1 surface relator abelianises to `(0,0)`.** Hence the\nabelian shadow of the NA-Stokes surface term is the identity: it adds\nnothing to any abelian/character-level functional (the combinatorial\nface of the trace-cyclicity prune). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.relatorExponentB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.relatorExponentB","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L92-L93","doc":"Exponent-sum in the `b` generator: `(+1) + (−1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.relatorExponentA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.relatorExponentA","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L88-L90","doc":"Exponent-sum of the commutator word `[a,b] = a b a⁻¹ b⁻¹` in the `a`\ngenerator: `(+1) + (−1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.rankH1_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.rankH1_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L71-L72","doc":"**`rank H₁ = 2`**: two handle generators `a₁, b₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.rankH1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.rankH1","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L67-L69","doc":"First-homology rank of a genus-`g` surface with one boundary component\nis `2g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifert_euler_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifert_euler_relation","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L61-L65","doc":"**The Euler relation `χ = 2 − 2g − b` holds** for the derived counts —\ni.e. `g = 1` is forced by `χ = −1`, `b = 1`. This is the genuine check\n(had the cell count been wrong, this would fail). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifertGenus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifertGenus","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L55-L59","doc":"Genus `g` of a connected surface with `b` boundary components satisfies\n`χ = 2 − 2g − b`. For the σ₁³ surface (`χ = −1`, `b = 1`) this pins\n`2g = 2 − b − χ = 2 − 1 − (−1) = 2`, i.e. `g = 1`. We record the genus\nand *verify the Euler relation closes* (the falsifiable content). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.boundaryComponents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.boundaryComponents","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L51-L53","doc":"The surface has **one** boundary component (the knot σ₁³ closure is a\nknot, not a link). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifertEuler_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifertEuler_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L48-L49","doc":"**`χ = −1`** for the σ₁³ Seifert surface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifertEuler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifertEuler","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L43-L46","doc":"Euler characteristic of the σ₁³ Seifert surface: `χ = #disks − #bands`\n(a 2-complex with `#disks` 2-cells glued along `#bands` 1-cells that\nconnect the two disks; the standard band-surface CW count). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifertBands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifertBands","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L40-L41","doc":"Number of twisted bands (1-cells): one per crossing of σ₁³. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifertDisks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.seifertDisks","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Sigma1CubedSeifertTessellation.lean#L36-L38","doc":"Number of Seifert disks (2-cells) from σ₁³: the 2 Seifert circles of a\n2-strand braid. ","signatureChunk":0}]}